rl":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":3,"closed_issues":3687,"state":"closed","created_at":"2024-12-19T08:51:28Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T21:48:38Z","due_on":"2025-09-15T00:00:00Z","closed_at":"2025-09-18T17:13:14Z"},"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-05-16T10:10:23Z","updated_at":"2026-05-10T01:06:42Z","closed_at":"2025-05-21T14:09:51Z","assignee":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in versions 4.4, 4.4.1, and 4.5 dev 4\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable.mono - Ubuntu 25.04 25.04 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2070 SUPER (nvidia; 570.133.07) - AMD Ryzen 5 3600 6-Core Processor (12 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\n## Issue\n\nWhen using Jolt Physics, having many overlapping `Area3D` nodes will result in a heavy performance penalty, **even if `monitorable` is disabled for all of them.**\n\nThis is not the case for Godot's default Physics Engine, which seems to disable collision checks between such pairs of areas like one would probably expect.\n\n## Cause\n\nLooking through the implementation, I found that this is most likely caused by `JoltArea3D` setting the `motion_type` of the underlying Jolt sensor body to `kinematic` [here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/c3ae6aa10b1c0c5488cf5b5e82dd34d265c1567c/modules/jolt_physics/objects/jolt_area_3d.cpp#L73C24-L73C50) regardless of its `monitoring` state. Like also stated in [the Jolt Physics library's documentation](https://jrouwe.github.io/JoltPhysics/class_body.html#a5d8e1f66eed163868a633cdb93859f77), this appears to be very costly in cases where there are many such overlapping areas, causing collision test times to explode with an increasing number of contacts. This seems unnecessary, as the area will just ignore the computed collisions afterwards anyway. \n\n## Potential Fixes\n\n### 1) Use Empty Collision Masks and Update Documentation\n\nWhile I found that this issue can also be circumvented by setting the collision mask to zero, I would still argue that this is unexpected behavior that should probably be fixed, or, at the very least, documented.\n\n### 2) Adjust the Source\n\nAs a possible improvement, I already tested modifying the source code to toggle the internal Jolt body's `motion_type` between `kinematic` and `static` based on the associated `monitoring` value, which seems to fix this issue. As far as I can tell from my experiments, my changes also do not seem to negatively impact the overall behavior of the area, i.e., non-monitoring areas can still be detected by monitoring ones and monitoring behavior is not affected at all. \n\nEdit: I created a PR in case this might be an acceptable fix: #106483 \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a new project. \n- Set 3D physics to Jolt.\n- Create a scene with *many* (this will likely depend on the used machine; in my case, around ~250 areas placed on top of each other nearly brings the game to a hold) overlapping fully configured, i.e., having a `CollisionShape3D` child, `Area3D` instances with `monitoring` disabled.\n- Run the scene and observe the frame rate/processing times via the debug monitor.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[joltarea3dperformanceissuedemo.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20241897/joltarea3dperformanceissuedemo.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106482/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106482/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}